Project: JobLens — ISM 6225 final project: job & internship scam shield for students and career
centers (ASP.NET Core MVC + MCP chatbot).
Stack (pinned, do not change versions): C#, .NET 10 (net10.0), ASP.NET Core MVC,
ModelContextProtocol.AspNetCore 2.2.0, Microsoft.Data.Sqlite 10.0.12,
Microsoft.Extensions.AI 10.10.0, Microsoft.Extensions.AI.OpenAI 10.10.0, OpenAI 2.14.0.
Do NOT use Entity Framework. Use ADO.NET with Microsoft.Data.Sqlite.

Domain: job/internship scam safety for students and university career centers (sample data).
Tables: Companies (PK CompanyId), ScamReports (PK ReportId, FK CompanyId → Companies), JobPostings, InterviewReviews, CheckLogs, Recruiters, Users, JobApplications (owner-only, FK UserId → Users), Resumes (one per user, redacted text only).
Live jobs come only from USAJOBS (ILiveJobsProvider → UsaJobsClient). Do not add other job providers.

Solution layout (Clean Architecture):
- src/JobLens.Domain — entities and domain constants (no package references)
- src/JobLens.Application — interfaces, DTOs, services, DI (AddApplication); depends only on Domain
- src/JobLens.Infrastructure — SQLite repositories, seed, external HTTP clients, AI factory, documents; depends on Application + Domain
- src/JobLens.Web — MVC Controllers, Views, ViewModels, wwwroot, Mcp tools, ChatOrchestrator, Program.cs
- tests/JobLens.Tests — xUnit tests referencing Domain, Application, Infrastructure, Web
- Solution file: JobLens.slnx

Dependency rule: Web → Application ← Infrastructure; Application → Domain.
Web may reference Infrastructure only for composition root (AddInfrastructure) and startup (DatabaseInitializer).
Controllers call Application services (or ChatOrchestrator); never repositories.
MCP tools call Application services/interfaces only. ChatOrchestrator never calls repositories.

Architecture rules:
- Request flow: Browser → MVC Controller → ChatOrchestrator → MCP client → HTTP /mcp → MCP tools → Application interfaces → Infrastructure repositories → SQLite.
- No SQL in controllers, Razor views, Application, or Domain. All SQL lives in src/JobLens.Infrastructure/Persistence.
- Every SQL command is parameterized ($param). Never concatenate user input into SQL.
- MCP tools are read-only, narrow, described, validated, and return bounded output (max 20 rows).
  Never create an execute_sql, run_query, or any arbitrary-SQL tool, and never add write tools to MCP.
- Writes (Create/Update/Delete) happen ONLY through MVC controllers → Application services (business rules) → repositories
  (parameterized SQL). Controllers stay thin; validation in ViewModels/Dtos + Services.
- ChatOrchestrator never calls the repository directly — only through MCP tools.
- SQLite file: App_Data/joblens.db under the Web project locally; HOME/data/JobLens/joblens.db on Azure. Never under wwwroot.
- Secrets (AI keys) only in dotnet user-secrets locally and Azure environment variables. Never in appsettings.json or Git.
- Every POST uses [ValidateAntiForgeryToken]. Server-side validation on all input. Friendly errors, details only in logs.
- AllowedHosts: localhost values in development; exact Azure hostname in production. Never "*".

UI rules (light theme, same look as our JobLens static prototype):
- CSS variables in wwwroot/css/site.css :root — bg #F8FAFC, surface #FFFFFF, border #E2E8F0, text #1E293B,
  muted #64748B, primary #3B82F6, primary-hover #2563EB, primary-light #DBEAFE,
  low #16A34A/#DCFCE7, medium #D97706/#FEF3C7, high #DC2626/#FEE2E2.
- Font Inter (Google Fonts). Rounded corners, soft shadows, generous spacing, responsive to 360px.
- No Bootstrap. No inline styles. Accessible labels, focus states, aria-live for chat transcript.

Code style: nullable enabled, file-scoped namespaces, sealed classes/records where sensible,
async with CancellationToken, short comments explaining WHY.
